Package: bad-ips
Version: 4.0.0
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: perl, nftables, jq, postgresql-client, libconfig-tiny-perl, libdbi-perl, libdbd-pg-perl, libjson-perl, libnet-cidr-perl, liblog-log4perl-perl, libfile-readbackwards-perl, libfile-slurp-perl, libregexp-common-perl, libwww-perl, liblwp-protocol-https-perl
Maintainer: Gardner <gardner@homelab>
Description: Distributed IP blocking system with a shared ban list (ALPHA)
 Bad IPs watches logs for attacks and blocks offending addresses with
 nftables, sharing bans between servers through one PostgreSQL ban list.
 .
 Role mode (4.0) is for a fleet behind one edge: report hosts watch their
 logs and report to the shared list, and the block host (the edge) drops
 listed addresses on chosen interfaces only. Rules count repeats within a
 window measured by each log line's own time, pin the client address to a
 fixed place in the line, and never touch never-block networks; bans survive
 nftables reloads and are lifted fleet-wide with `bad_ips unban`.
 .
 Without a role configured, the 3.x daemon runs exactly as before.
 .
 ALPHA STATUS: This software is currently in alpha testing. While actively
 tested on live production servers, use with appropriate caution.
Homepage: https://github.com/permittivity2/bad-ips
